## Students & Classes

The **Students** and **Classes** sections are where office staff maintain the roster: adding new
students, assigning them to a class, and updating their records. This is separate from
**Admissions**, which covers a prospective student's application before they're enrolled — once
an application is approved, the record graduates into the regular student roster.

## Teachers

The **Teachers** section lists all staff, and is where a school admin:

- Adds or edits a teacher's profile
- Assigns a teacher to one or more classes (this assignment is what determines a teacher's
  attendance-editing access — see [Taking Attendance](/docs/shared-staff-attendance-overview))
- Views a teacher's monthly attendance
- Sets up **substitutions** when a class's regular teacher is away

## Substitutions

A substitution temporarily changes who has editable access to a class's attendance and related
records, without permanently reassigning the class. If a teacher unexpectedly can't edit a class
they normally can, or a substitute can't see a class they were told to cover, check whether the
substitution was actually recorded here — it's a common source of confusion since the effect
(access changing) isn't visible from the attendance screen itself.

## Admissions bridge

The **Admissions** entry under Students links out to the same guidebook and applicant-portal
flow that prospective parents use before they apply — see
[Applying to a School](/docs/admissions-applying) for the applicant-facing side of this.
